, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1315281600", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "22418891", "author": {"steamid": "76561198058854733", "personaname": "Wølf", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/SchwarzerWolffe/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 52, "playtime_forever": 2012, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 1602, "last_played": 1490391357, "avatar": "9494db00d80d441b08c3c4303dd7b30cb16b3714"}, "language": "english", "review": "Surely a masterpiece that the Emperor can look upon with pride.\n\nWarhammer 40,000: Space Marine is a fun, action packed, third-person shooter that takes you into the grim future filled with war.\n\nIt is one of the best Warhammer games to date. Infact I'm surprised Games Workshop haven't released a sequel to this GLORIOUS PIECE OF WORK! This is the kind of game we want from you GW not f***ing chess games.\n\nAs story goes, you play as Captain Titus of the Ultra s̶m̶u̶r̶f̶s̶ marines tasked with leading his squad as a supportive vanguard for Imperial Guardsman who are having trouble dealing with an Ork invasion, as the story progresses you will eventually encounter a threat that is greater than a mere Ork invasion.\n\nIt really is an immersive experience, the multiplayer is fantastic even though the community has died out a little it isn't uncommon to find a full lobby. The coolest thing is that you can customize your character, matching your Space Marine to your tastes.\n\nThe Adeptus Ministorum, the Adepta Sororitas and the Inquisition approve of this marvellous game.", "timestamp_created": 1460678624, "timestamp_updated": 1460678624, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 14, "votes_funny": 3, "weighted_vote_score": "0.693718016147613525", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_acces